   "ruling": "Ruling: finding; medium; the model is right that line 1a adds every W-2 box 1 amount with no carve-out for wages earned while an inmate. i1040gi p. 23, Line 1a: \"If you earned wages while you were an inmate in a penal institution, report these amounts on Schedule 1, line 8u. Do not report these wages on line 1a.\" Earlier rounds ruled this scope because s1.line8_other refused 8u; lane x2-s1o removed s1.inmate_wages from that refusal and computes line 8u, so nothing now keeps inmate pay shown on a W-2 off line 1a (double count with 8u, or EIC earned income that p596 excludes). The nonqualified deferred compensation / section 457 pension part of the model's reason stays refused (s1.line8_other still names 8t). (BUG-0766)",
